---
name: conversation-image-scenes
description: Author an image for the current conversation while preserving permanent appearance and the recorded day.
---

For a conversation image, write your own complete scene: people, activity,
setting, clothing, pose, expression, gaze, lighting and camera. Imagined scenes
and image-only outfits do not update your presence or wardrobe. Recorded context
is available when useful, but does not constrain a clearly imagined picture.
Do not invent real facts about the human.

Read context when needed:
`{{IMAGE_COMMAND}} context`

Preview without rendering:
`{{IMAGE_COMMAND}} preview --prompt "YOUR OWN COMPLETE SCENE"`

Generate with the native renderer:
`{{IMAGE_COMMAND}} generate --prompt "YOUR OWN COMPLETE SCENE"`

Execute directly by calling the `terminal` tool function. NEVER print the shell command into chat with the human. When the command returns with `send: MEDIA:...`, include that `MEDIA:<path>` line on its own line in your reply. For longer prompts use `--request` with a JSON file
containing `prompt` and optional `width`, `height`, `seed` and `preset`. Choose
framing and dimensions deliberately. The helper automatically adds the entire
permanent appearance unchanged; do not shorten or replace it. Other pictured
people have their own appearance. Existing eligibility and review preferences
apply; use `--intimate` only when eligible. A refusal is not a reason to switch
generators. Never guess an output path or claim delivery without a real result.
Share the returned `MEDIA:` path only when sending is authorized.

Scheduled photos retain the default recorded-photo prompt and workflow. Do not
replace their jobs with this conversation route or rewrite the day for a picture.
